The three read-only e-Stat tools were rewritten in Common Lisp against Nodecode's cell contract: the
same host (api.e-stat.go.jp), the same three endpoints (getStatsList, getMetaInfo, getStatsData),
the same application ID, the same name-to-code lookup for areas, periods and categories, and the
same citation with every figure. What the original answered as JSON strings, this answers as a block
of lines a model reads. Left out: the original's ranking heuristics and its warning passes over
base years, preliminary figures and missing items, which were tuned to Python callers; the rewrite
still flags a preliminary table and says when a selection is wider than the row cap, and keeps the
metadata cache of the original. The tool descriptions no longer tell the model to avoid web search,
since a Nodecode cell does not own that choice.
